{"title":"2023 IOQM/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The ex-radii of a triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/30299c180db7406f0d4a1409dcde323630ff0229.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\nIf the sides of the triangle are the roots of the cubic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44d68235be5c84eac0444af4ddf4b82ee2292b19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - px^2 + qx - r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" /> , where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are integers, find the integer\nnearest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f136e06b483222770e3ab899b454c9889ea706b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{p+q+r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017090800\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.003 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.003 seconds\nPreprocessor visited nod